# Components

Rules for files under `app/components/`. Follow global rules in `global.mdc` for TypeScript, JSDoc, and formatting.

## Purpose

Components are **reusable UI building blocks** extracted from pages when markup or behavior is shared across routes. Pages orchestrate data; components render and emit events.

## Directory Structure

```
app/components/
├── NoDataCard.vue              # Shared empty-state card
├── ResultCommand.vue           # Shared result/export panel
├── CreateCommandButton.vue     # Action button with encapsulated logic
├── navbar.vue                  # App chrome (prefer layouts for shell UI)
└── modals/
    └── DeviceEdit.vue          # Dialog/modal components
```

- Place **modals and dialogs** under `modals/`.
- Group related components in subfolders by feature when the set grows (e.g. `devices/`, `agents/`).
- Prefer **PascalCase** filenames for multi-word components (`NoDataCard.vue`, `DeviceEdit.vue`).

## Naming

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Presentational | PascalCase, noun-based | `NoDataCard.vue`, `ResultCommand.vue` |
| Action/control | PascalCase, describes action | `CreateCommandButton.vue` |
| Modals | PascalCase under `modals/` | `modals/DeviceEdit.vue` |

- Nuxt auto-registers components; import explicitly when clarity helps:

```ts
import NoDataCard from '~/components/NoDataCard.vue'
import DeviceEditDialog from '~/components/modals/DeviceEdit.vue'
```

## File Structure

Every component follows this block order:

```vue
<template>
  <!-- markup -->
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
// imports → props/emits → state → composables → handlers
</script>

<style scoped></style>
```

- Use a **single** `<script setup lang="ts">` block — no mixed Options API.
- Add `scoped` styles only when the component needs local CSS.

## Props and Emits

Use typed `defineProps` and `defineEmits`. Provide defaults for optional props.

```ts
interface ResultCommandProps {
  exportBtn?: boolean
  isLoadingDataSingle?: boolean
  queryStatus?: boolean
  singleDataContent?: string
}

const props = withDefaults(defineProps<ResultCommandProps>(), {
  exportBtn: false,
  isLoadingDataSingle: false,
  queryStatus: false,
  singleDataContent: '',
})
```

### v-model pattern (modals/dialogs)

```ts
interface DeviceEditProps {
  isVisible: boolean
  deviceDataRef: DeviceData
  isPublished: boolean
  isUpdatingPending: boolean
}

const props = defineProps<DeviceEditProps>()

const emit = defineEmits<{
  'update:isVisible': [value: boolean]
  'update:isPublished': [value: boolean]
  updateDevice: [payload: DeviceUpdatePayload]
}>()
```

```vue
<v-dialog :model-value="isVisible" @update:model-value="emit('update:isVisible', $event)">
  <!-- dialog content -->
</v-dialog>
```

- Use **`update:propName`** for two-way binding (`v-model:is-visible`).
- Keep a local ref synced with props via `watch` when the child mutates display state.
- Emit domain events (`updateDevice`) instead of mutating parent data directly.

## Component Categories

### Presentational components

Display data passed via props; minimal logic.

- Examples: `NoDataCard`, `ResultCommand`
- Accept text/content/loading flags as props.
- Use i18n for labels (`$vuetify.locale.t(...)` or project i18n).
- Delegate formatting/export to `~/utils/**` (e.g. `jsonToCsv`, `downloadExcel`).

```vue
<template>
  <v-card rounded="lg" class="elevation-2 pa-3">
    <v-card-title class="d-flex justify-center">
      <h4>{{ $vuetify.locale.t('component.noDataAvailable') }}</h4>
    </v-card-title>
    <v-card-text class="text-center">
      <p>{{ promptText }}</p>
    </v-card-text>
  </v-card>
</template>
```

### Action components

Encapsulate user actions that call composables.

- Examples: `CreateCommandButton`
- Accept configuration props (`commandContent`, `tooltipText`).
- Use mutation composables internally (`useCreateCommandByDeviceId`).
- Confirm destructive/create actions with a dialog (e.g. SweetAlert) before mutating.
- Expose loading via composable `isPending` on the button.

### Modal components

Overlay dialogs for edit/create flows.

- Live under `modals/`.
- Control visibility via `v-model:is-visible` from the parent page.
- Receive entity data as props; emit save/update payloads to the parent.
- Parent page or composable performs the actual API mutation.

## Script Conventions

1. **Imports** — Vue APIs, composables, utils, types, child components.
2. **Props / emits** — typed interfaces with defaults.
3. **Local state** — `ref` / `reactive` for UI-only state.
4. **Composables** — mutations/queries when the component owns the action.
5. **Handlers** — named functions for clicks, export, confirm, close.
6. **Lifecycle / watchers** — sync props to local state when needed.

```ts
const localIsPublished = ref(props.isPublished)

watch(
  () => props.isPublished,
  (newValue) => {
    localIsPublished.value = newValue
  },
)
```

## Dependencies

| Layer | Allowed in components |
|-------|------------------------|
| `~/composables/**` | Yes — for action components |
| `~/utils/**` | Yes — formatting, export, helpers |
| `~/components/**` | Yes — compose smaller components |
| i18n / UI library | Yes |
| `~/services/**` directly | Avoid — prefer composables |
| Route middleware / `definePageMeta` | No |
| Layout shells (`v-app`, nav drawers) | Prefer layouts, not components |

## Composition

- Compose smaller components inside larger ones (`NoDataCard` uses `CreateCommandButton`).
- Pass **narrow props** (strings, booleans, IDs) rather than entire stores when possible.
- Use slots when the parent must inject variable markup; use props when data is structured.

## Template Conventions

- Wrap grouped content in cards/panels consistent with the design system.
- Show loading indicators (`v-progress-linear`) when `isLoading` props are true.
- Use tooltips on icon/action buttons for accessibility.
- Keep templates declarative; move JSON parsing, export, and validation to script or utils.

## What Belongs in Components

- Empty states reused across pages (`NoDataCard`).
- Result panels, export toolbars, data viewers (`ResultCommand`).
- Modals/dialogs (`DeviceEdit`).
- Buttons/controls with repeated mutation + confirm flows.
- Any UI block duplicated across 2+ pages.

## What Not to Put in Components

- Full page layouts (use `app/layouts/`).
- Route definitions or middleware.
- One-off markup used in a single page with no reuse.
- Direct REST calls — wrap in composables first.
- Mixed `<script setup>` and Options API in the same file.

## Adding a New Component

1. Identify duplicated UI or behavior across pages.
2. Choose location: root `app/components/` or subfolder (`modals/`, `{feature}/`).
3. Define typed props/emits interfaces.
4. Keep data fetching in composables; pass results in as props or use action composables inside.
5. Import in pages with `~/components/...` when explicit imports aid readability.
6. Add JSDoc on non-trivial exported helpers used by the component.
